.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes a feed for each rules file in the rules directory.
A rules file names a page,
which can be HTML or XML (such as another feed),
and says what to extract from it,
how to change what it extracts and which entries to keep.
.Nm
fetches the page,
extracts the feed’s information and entries,
and writes the feed as Atom or as RSS for podcasts.
.Pp
The feed for
.Ql "<rules-dir>/<name>\&.wattle"
is written to
.Ql "<output-dir>/<name>\&.xml" .
It is written to a temporary file in the output directory and
renamed into place,
so a reader never sees part of a feed.
The output directory is created if it does not exist.
.Pp
Each feed is made in turn.
A feed that fails,
because its page cannot be fetched,
its status is not 2xx or its rules file has an error,
is reported on standard error as
.Ql "colander: <name>: <reason>"
and its file is left as it was.
The other feeds are still made.
A feed with no entries is written,
with a warning,
since that usually means that its page has changed.
.Pp
.Nm
prints nothing else,
so it can be run from cron.
.
