.Sh RULES FILES
A rules file is a Wattle program that defines
.Ql "feed" ,
a map.
It is compiled in an environment of its own,
so it can define other bindings for its own use,
and it can use Wattle’s standard library.
Of
.Nm
‘s own functions it has
.Ql "extract" ,
.Ql "header"
and those that begin with
.Ql "markup/" ,
.Ql "date/" ,
.Ql "select/"
and
.Ql "template/" .
.Pp
A rules file is code:
.Nm
runs it.
Use rules files that you have written or read.
.Pp
The keys of
.Ql "feed"
are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":url"
.Xc
The page to fetch,
a string that begins with
.Ql "http://"
or
.Ql "https://" .
Required.
.It Xo
.Ql ":format"
.Xc
How to read the page,
.Ql ":html"
(the default)
or
.Ql ":xml" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":template"
.Xc
How to write the feed:
.Ql ":atom"
(the default),
.Ql ":podcast" ,
or a function.
See
.Sx "TEMPLATES" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":info"
.Xc
The feed’s own elements,
as a vector of
.Ql "\(lBname value\(rB"
pairs.
.It Xo
.Ql ":entries"
.Xc
An
.Ql "extract"
rule that selects each entry’s element in the page.
.It Xo
.Ql ":entry"
.Xc
Each entry’s elements,
as a vector of
.Ql "\(lBname value\(rB"
pairs.
.It Xo
.Ql ":keep?"
.Xc
A function of an entry that returns true to keep it.
.It Xo
.Ql ":transform"
.Xc
A function from an entry to the entry to write.
.It Xo
.Ql ":headers"
.Xc
A map of request headers to send,
such as
.Ql "{\(dqUser-Agent\(dq \(dq\&.\&.\&.\(dq}" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":timeout"
.Xc
The seconds to wait for the page.
This defaults to 30.
.El
.Pp
A name is a keyword,
such as
.Ql ":title"
or
.Ql ":itunes:image" ;
it is the name of the element written.
A value is a string,
an
.Ql "extract"
rule or a
.Ql "header"
rule.
The elements are written in the order of the pairs.
.Pp
With
.Ql ":entries" ,
the rules in
.Ql ":entry"
select within each entry’s element.
Without it,
each rule in
.Ql ":entry"
selects every match in the page,
and the first match of each goes to the first entry,
the second to the second,
and so on.
.Pp
.Ql ":keep?"
and
.Ql ":transform"
are given each entry as a map of names to strings,
such as
.Ql "{:title \(dq\&.\&.\&.\(dq :link \(dq\&.\&.\&.\(dq}" .
.Ql ":keep?"
is called first.
A transform can change,
add or remove values.
Values that it adds are written after the others,
in order of name.
.
.Sh EXTRACTING
.Ql "\*(lpextract selector & options\*(rp"
returns a rule that takes a value from the first element that
.Ar selector
matches.
The selector is searched for in the entry’s element,
or in the whole page for a rule in
.Ql ":info"
or with
.Ql ":absolute" .
An empty selector is the entry’s element itself.
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":content"
.Xc
What to take from the element:
.Ql ":text"
(the default,
its text with the surrounding whitespace removed),
.Ql ":inner-html"
(its contents as markup),
or
.Ql ":html"
or
.Ql ":xml"
(the element itself as markup,
such as an
.Ql "enclosure" ) .
.It Xo
.Ql ":attr"
.Xc
The name of an attribute to take instead,
such as
.Ql "\(dqhref\(dq" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":absolute"
.Xc
When true,
search the whole page rather than the entry’s element.
.It Xo
.Ql ":process"
.Xc
A function of the value and the rule that returns a string.
.It Xo
.Ql ":prefix" ,
.Ql ":suffix"
.Xc
Strings to add before and after the value.
.It Xo
.Ql ":type"
.Xc
.Ql ":datetime"
reads the value as a date and writes it in the form of RFC 3339
(see
.Sx "DATES" ) ,
or as an empty string if it is not a date.
.Ql ":cdata"
writes the value in a CDATA section,
for a value that is HTML.
.El
.Pp
The steps are applied in that order:
content,
process,
prefix and suffix,
type.
A rule that matches nothing gives an empty string,
without its prefix or suffix.
.Pp
.Ql "\*(lpheader name & options\*(rp"
returns a rule that takes the value of the response header
.Ar name ,
in any case,
such as
.Ql "\(dqLast-Modified\(dq" .
It takes
.Ql ":process" ,
.Ql ":prefix" ,
.Ql ":suffix"
and
.Ql ":type" .
.
.Sh SELECTORS
Selectors are a subset of CSS:
type selectors (\c
.Ql "div" ,
.Ql "*" ) ,
.Ql "\&.class" ,
.Ql "#id" ,
.Ql "\(lBattr\(rB" ,
.Ql "\(lBattr=v\(rB" ,
.Ql "\(lBattr~=v\(rB" ,
.Ql "\(lBattr^=v\(rB" ,
.Ql "\(lBattr$=v\(rB"
and
.Ql "\(lBattr*=v\(rB" ,
the descendant combinator (a space)
and the child combinator (\c
.Ql ">" ) ,
and lists separated by
.Ql "\&," .
.Ql "ns|type"
matches the element
.Ql "ns:type"
in XML,
such as
.Ql "itunes|image" .
Any other selector is an error.
.Pp
HTML is read leniently,
and tag and attribute names are lowercased,
so write HTML selectors in lower case.
XML names are kept as written.
.
.Sh TEMPLATES
Each value is written according to its rule:
escaped,
in a CDATA section (\c
.Ql ":type :cdata" )
or as it is (\c
.Ql ":content :html"
or
.Ql ":xml" ) .
.Pp
.Ql ":atom"
writes an Atom feed with the
.Ql ":info"
elements and an
.Ql "entry"
element for each entry.
.Ql ":author"
is written as
.Ql "<author><name>\&.\&.\&.</name></author>"
and
.Ql ":link"
as
.Ql "<link href=\(dq\&.\&.\&.\(dq rel=\(dqalternate\(dq />" .
A CDATA value in
.Ql "title" ,
.Ql "subtitle" ,
.Ql "summary" ,
.Ql "content"
or
.Ql "rights"
is marked
.Ql "type=\(dqhtml\(dq" .
.Pp
.Ql ":podcast"
writes an RSS 2.0 feed with the iTunes namespace:
a
.Ql "channel"
with the
.Ql ":info"
elements and an
.Ql "item"
for each entry.
.Ql ":itunes:category"
is written as
.Ql "<itunes:category text=\(dq\&.\&.\&.\(dq/>" ,
.Ql ":itunes:image"
as
.Ql "<itunes:image href=\(dq\&.\&.\&.\(dq/>"
and
.Ql ":guid"
with
.Ql "isPermaLink=\(dqfalse\(dq" .
.Pp
A function given as
.Ql ":template"
is called with a map of
.Ql ":info"
and
.Ql ":entries" .
.Ql ":info"
is a vector of
.Ql "\(lBname value mode\(rB"
triples,
where mode is
.Ql ":text" ,
.Ql ":cdata"
or
.Ql ":markup" ,
and
.Ql ":entries"
is a vector of such vectors.
It returns the feed as a string.
.
.Sh DATES
.Ql ":type :datetime"
reads dates written as
.Ql "2026-11-23"
or
.Ql "2026-11-23T08:00:00+09:00" ,
.Ql "Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0900"
(or with a zone such as
.Ql "GMT" ) ,
.Ql "November 23, 2026" ,
.Ql "23 November 2026"
and
.Ql "11/23/2026" .
Months and days of the week can be written in full or in three
letters.
A date with an offset keeps it;
a date without one is in the local time zone,
and a date without a time is midnight.
.
.Sh FETCHING
.Nm
sends a GET request with the User-Agent
.Ql "Colander/<version> \*(lp+https://github\&.com/pyrmont/colander\*(rp" ,
which
.Ql ":headers"
can replace.
It follows up to five redirects,
accepts gzip and deflate,
and reads at most 16 MiB of a response.
It uses the system’s certificates for HTTPS.
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with 0 if every feed was made,
and with 1 if any feed failed,
its options are invalid or the rules directory cannot be read.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A rules file,
.Ql "rules/essays\&.wattle" ,
for a page that lists essays:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*(lpdef- url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/essays\&.html\(dq\*(rp

\*(lpdef- link \*(lpextract \(dqa\(dq :attr \(dqhref\(dq :prefix \(dqhttps://example\&.org\(dq\*(rp\*(rp

\*(lpdef feed
  {:url url
   :info \(lB\(lB:id url\(rB
          \(lB:updated \*(lpheader \(dqLast-Modified\(dq :type :datetime\*(rp\(rB
          \(lB:title \(dqEssays\(dq\(rB
          \(lB:author \(dqA\&. Writer\(dq\(rB\(rB
   :entries \*(lpextract \(dqul\&.posts > li\(dq\*(rp
   :entry \(lB\(lB:id link\(rB
           \(lB:title \*(lpextract \(dqa\(dq\*(rp\(rB
           \(lB:link link\(rB\(rB}\*(rp
.Ed
.Pp
A rules file that filters another feed and changes its titles:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*(lpdef feed
  {:url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/podcast\&.xml\(dq
   :format :xml
   :template :podcast
   :info \(lB\(lB:title \(dqOne Segment\(dq\(rB
          \(lB:link \(dqhttps://example\&.org/\(dq\(rB\(rB
   :entries \*(lpextract \(dqitem\(dq\*(rp
   :entry \(lB\(lB:title \*(lpextract \(dqtitle\(dq\*(rp\(rB
           \(lB:description \*(lpextract \(dqdescription\(dq :type :cdata\*(rp\(rB
           \(lB:enclosure \*(lpextract \(dqenclosure\(dq :content :xml\*(rp\(rB
           \(lB:guid \*(lpextract \(dqguid\(dq\*(rp\(rB\(rB
   :keep? \*(lpfn \(lBe\(rB \*(lpstring/find \(dqSegment\(dq \*(lpe :title\*(rp\*(rp\*(rp
   :transform \*(lpfn \(lBe\(rB
                \*(lpassoc e :title \*(lpstring/replace-all \(dq | Show\(dq \(dq\(dq \*(lpe :title\*(rp\*(rp\*(rp\*(rp}\*(rp
.Ed
.Pp
Make every feed in
.Ql "rules"
and write them to
.Ql "/var/www/feeds" :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ colander -o /var/www/feeds
.Ed
.Pp
Run every two hours from cron:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
0 */2 * * * cd /srv/feeds && $HOME/bin/colander -o public
.Ed
.Pp
Check one feed without writing a file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ colander -O -i essays
.Ed
